      "text": "To determine the total number of games played in the league, we first recognize that each game involves two teams. If the total number of games played is \\( G \\), given there are nine teams, we calculate the total game count as follows:\n\n1. For any given team, it plays three games with the teams it faces directly.\n2. There are eight teams to which each of these active teams plays exactly three games (since each team interacts with the other fewer seven).\n3. Hence, for every team, the number of unique games played totals \\( 3 \\times \\text{number of unique games faced per team} = 3 \\times 8 = 24 \\).\n4. With 9 teams, the total games, assuming no doubles or other combos involve different matching teams, is \\( G = 24 \\times 9 / 2 \\). We realize dividing by two is what accounts for repetitions.\n5. Thus, the total number of games played is:\n   - \\(\\frac{24 \\times 9}{2} = 108\\)\n   where \\(\\frac{24}{2}\\) eliminates the double-counted overlaps.\n\nTherefore, the total number of games played during the season is \\(\\boxed{108}\\).",
